Subject: [PATCH] physmap: map no-gpio mtd-rom at its exact resource size (#45)

Upstream rounds the window down (not up) to BIT(fls64(size)-1) so the
aperture is power-of-two sized; that rounding only exists for the
addr-gpios windowing (physmap_addr_gpios_*).  With no addr-gpios the
extra bit is never consumed, so a non-pow2 reg (the 7 MiB mtd-rom
rootfs partition) loses its tail instead of gaining stale mapping.

Keep win_order + BIT() sizing when info->gpios is present; otherwise
take resource_size(res) verbatim.
---
 drivers/mtd/maps/physmap-core.c | 11 +++++++----
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/mtd/maps/physmap-core.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/maps/physmap-core.c
@@ -522,10 +522,13 @@
 		if (!info->maps[i].phys)
 			info->maps[i].phys = res->start;

-		info->win_order = fls64(resource_size(res)) - 1;
-		info->maps[i].size = BIT(info->win_order +
-					 (info->gpios ?
-					  info->gpios->ndescs : 0));
+		if (info->gpios) {
+			info->win_order = fls64(resource_size(res)) - 1;
+			info->maps[i].size = BIT(info->win_order +
+						 info->gpios->ndescs);
+		} else {
+			info->maps[i].size = resource_size(res);
+		}

 		info->maps[i].map_priv_1 = (unsigned long)dev;
